# 🚨 DEPLOYMENT GATE — READ BEFORE EVERY TASK

**ALL WORK IS LOCAL BY DEFAULT.**

## DO NOT (until authorized)

- `git push` (any remote/branch)
- Deploy / publish to Mintlify production
- Trigger production deployment (GitHub Actions, Mintlify, dashboard “publish”)
- Modify live documentation / production DNS / live domain config
- Merge a production PR or create a production release

**unless the operator explicitly says exactly:**

```text
start the deployment process
```

## These do NOT authorize push or deploy

`fix this` · `complete this` · `finish` · `test` · `make it ready` · `prepare` · `update the documentation` · `resolve` · `verify` · `build` · `production ready` · `prepare for deployment` · `get it ready for live` · `check the deployment` · `commit the changes` · passing tests · clean working tree · “looks safe”

Completing a task is **not** deployment permission. Do **not** ask “Should I deploy?” — wait for the exact phrase.

## Local-only mode (default)

Allowed: inspect, edit, local Mintlify preview, local validate/tests/Playwright, screenshots, diffs, local backups.

Commits: only when the operator **explicitly** asks to commit. A local commit is **not** push permission.

## When authorized (`start the deployment process`)

Follow the full safe workflow in `docs/deployment/deploy.md` and `.cursor/skills/t3planet-deploy/SKILL.md`:

backup → verify Nitsan identity → verify `origin` = `nitsan-technologies/T3Planet-docs` · `master` → fetch/compare → preserve work → diff review → validate → commit as Nitsan → push `origin` → Mintlify verify → production QA → report.

Never force-push `master`. Never skip QA after push.

## Production source

```text
https://github.com/nitsan-technologies/T3Planet-docs.git
branch: master
live: https://docs.t3planet.de/en/latest
```

## End of local task report

```text
Changes completed locally: YES/NO
Local tests completed: YES/NO / NOT RUN
Local build/validate completed: YES/NO / NOT RUN
Production deployment started: NO
Git push performed: NO
Live documentation changed: NO
```

If ready: *The changes are ready locally. No Git push or production deployment was performed because deployment permission has not been provided.*
